---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Card from '../components/shared/Card.astro';
import SignalBadge from '../components/shared/SignalBadge.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/url.js';

const story = [
  ['Buyer', 'The Coastal Hotel posts an order for 120 kg okra, 10 weeks before it needs it.', '/buyer'],
  ['Farmer', 'Binta dials *1234# on a basic phone: "Okra: GOOD - buyer waiting". Tomato: DON\'T PLANT, too many kafos grow it.', '/farmer'],
  ['Kafo leader', 'Fatou types how many kg her kafo can grow and sees the expected cash before accepting. She assigns members and logs the beds for the hotel. Okra turns CAREFUL for the kafos nearby, so they don\'t all plant it.', '/kafo'],
  ['Admin', 'Three farmers report insects: okra WATCH OUT. A heavy-rain bulletin: ACT NOW by SMS, and Binta\'s phone rings with a voice alert.', '/admin'],
  ['Admin', 'Jump +8 weeks. Fatou checks the okra off as Ready, then Harvested, entering the kg each time. The hotel\'s forecast updates by itself.', '/admin#demo'],
  ['Kafo leader', 'Fatou weighs each member\'s okra and sends it with a proof photo. At the hotel she enters the buyer\'s 4-digit handover code.', '/kafo'],
  ['Buyer', 'The hotel checks the kg and pays: every woman is paid directly and gets a PAID SMS. The order log shows every step with its date.', '/buyer#orders'],
];
---
<Base title="About">
  <section class="mb-8 max-w-3xl">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted">UTG ITCA Hackathon 2026 · Challenge 02</p>
    <h1 class="mt-1 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Kafo Signal</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-lg">
      Women's garden groups (kafos) around Brikama all plant tomato at the same time, prices crash, and the harvest rots.
      Buyers like hotels can't find steady okra or pepper. Kafo Signal gives every kafo three simple signals,
      <strong>what to plant</strong>, <strong>where to sell</strong> and <strong>what risk is coming</strong>, and lets buyers order <strong>before planting</strong>.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      <SignalBadge signal="green" label="Good to plant" />
      <SignalBadge signal="yellow" label="Careful" />
      <SignalBadge signal="red" label="Don't plant" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="mb-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
    <Card>
      <h2 class="font-semibold">Any phone works</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted">Basic phones get words, not colours: the *1234# text menu, SMS from 1234, and a free voice call-back on *4321# in Mandinka, Wolof, Fula, Jola or English.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card>
      <h2 class="font-semibold">The leader keeps the record</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted">The kafo leader logs plantings and accepts orders in a simple app. Harvest dates and kg fill in from the crop calendar; scales at delivery make the numbers real.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card>
      <h2 class="font-semibold">Paid directly, by the kg</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted">Each member is paid to her own mobile wallet for the kg she delivered. The leader never holds group money; every member gets an SMS.</p>
    </Card>
  </div>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold">How the signal works</h2>
    <ul class="grid gap-3 text-sm md:grid-cols-3">
      <li class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface p-4"><strong>Plant:</strong> expected harvest ÷ demand in the district (baseline + buyer orders). Below 0.8 green, up to 1.3 yellow, above red.</li>
      <li class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface p-4"><strong>Sell:</strong> each market's price minus transport, compared with the 4-week average. A confirmed buyer order is always green.</li>
      <li class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface p-4"><strong>Risk:</strong> admin alerts from weather bulletins, plus farmers' pest reports. Unchecked reports can only make it yellow; red needs the leader to confirm.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold">The 3-minute demo</h2>
    <p class="mb-3 text-sm text-muted">Open the four pages side by side and press <strong>Reset demo</strong> first. Changes in one tab show in the others straight away.</p>
    <ol class="space-y-2">
      {story.map(([who, what, path], i) => (
        <li class="flex gap-3 rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface p-3 text-sm">
          <span class="flex h-8 w-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-brand font-bold text-brand-ink">{i + 1}</span>
          <span><a href={href(path)} class="font-semibold underline">{who}</a>: {what}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-4 max-w-3xl text-sm text-muted">
    <h2 class="mb-2 text-base font-semibold text-ink">What is real and what is simulated</h2>
    <p>Everything runs in the browser with demo data (names, phone numbers, prices and buyers are made up). USSD, SMS and voice calls are simulated on the farmer page; going live needs a server, a short code from PURA and an agreement with a mobile operator. Voice notes play in English until the team's recordings are added.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
